ious <italic>Borrelia</italic></article-title><source>Infect Immun</source><year>2002</year><volume>70</volume><fpage>4851</fpage><lpage>4858</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12183529</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b27"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lawrenz</surname><given-names>MB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effects of <italic>vlsE</italic> complementation on the infectivity of <italic>Borrelia burgdorferi</italic> lacking the linear plasmid lp28-1</article-title><source>Infect Immun</source><year>2004</year><volume>72</volume><fpage>6577</fpage><lpage>6585</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15501789</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b28"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name></person-group><article-title><italic>Borrelia burgdorferi</italic> lacking BBK32, a fibronectin-binding protein, retains full pathogenicity</article-title><source>Infect Immun</source><year>2006</year><volume>74</volume><fpage>3305</fpage><lpage>3313</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16714558</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b29"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McDowell</surname><given-names>JV</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Analysis of mechanisms associated with loss of infectivity of clonal populations of <italic>Borrelia burgdorferi</italic> B31 MI</article-title><source>Infect Immun</source><year>2001</year><volume>69</volume><fpage>3670</fpage><lpage>3677</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11349029</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b30"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McDowell</surname><given-names>JV</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evidence that the variable regions of the central domain of VlsE are antigenic during infection with Lyme disease spirochetes<